<p>These remains were discovered in 2009 by archaeologists in Modena, Italy. They&#8217;re believed to have been buried between the 4th and 6th century AD. At first they were thought to be a male and a female, but it&#8217;s now been confirmed that they&#8217;re both male.</p>
<p>They were buried with their hands interlocked. They&#8217;re now on display at the Civic Museum of Modena.</p>
